Column name: bom_r64_ne Type: NUMBER Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; hurricane-force (33m/s) or above. Northeast quadrant
Column name: bom_r34_se Type: NUMBER Description: This is the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; gale-force (17m/s) or above. The four sectors show the mean extent in the respective quadrant centred on the cardinal point. Southeast quadrant
Column name: usa_r50_nw Type: NUMBER Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: tokyo_latitude Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: usa_r50_se Type: NUMBER Description: – 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: wellington_latitude Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: usa_roci Type: NUMBER Description: radius of the last closed isobar/n0 - 999 n mi. NOT BEST TRACKED (not reanalyzed)
Column name: td9635_wind Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: usa_agency Type: TEXT Description: The agency file providing the information: The representative US agency data is derived from a hierarchical selection: the first dataset in the following list to provide information at the given time is used as the USA_agency: - HURDAT_ATL - HURSAT_EPA - ATCF (for NA and EP basins only) - JTWC_WP - JTWC_IO - JTWC_EP - JTWC_CP - JTWC_SH - CPHC [separate file provided by CPHC for years TBD] - tcvitals - THIS INDICATES THAT THE DATA ARE PRELIMINARY While these agencies are generally orthogonal/nthere are cases where a system is provided in more than one source. In this case/nthe report from the highest source is used. ATCF format info from: https://www.nrlmry.navy.mil/atcf_web/docs/database/new/abdeck.txt HURDAT2 info from: http://www.nhc.noaa.gov/data/hurdat/hurdat2-format-atlantic.pdf
Column name: landfall Type: NUMBER Description: Nearest location to land within next 6 hours. This can be thought of a landfall flag: =0 -- Landfall within 6 hours. >0 -- No landfall within next 6 hours. Calculations are based on storm center (columns 9,10). Values less than 60 nmile likely are impacted by the system even though the center of the system is not over land. The uses the same land mask as DIST2LAND.
Column name: usa_longitude Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: wmo_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: td9635_longitude Type: FLOAT Description: Longitude from Dataset of a collection of western Pacific Storms (~1945-1976)
Column name: latitude Type: FLOAT Description: 
Column name: usa_status Type: TEXT Description: Status of system. Options are:  DB - disturbance/n TD - tropical depression/n TS - tropical storm/n TY - typhoon/n ST - super typhoon/n TC - tropical cyclone/n HU,HR - hurricane/n SD - subtropical depression/n SS - subtropical storm/n EX - extratropical systems/n PT - post tropical/n IN - inland/n DS - dissipating/n LO - low/n WV - tropical wave/n ET - extrapolated/n MD - monsoon depression/n XX - unknown.
Column name: nadi_wind Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: sid Type: TEXT Description: Storm Identifier.
Column name: usa_r34_sw Type: NUMBER Description: – 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: wmo_wind Type: NUMBER Description: Maximum sustained wind speed from the WMO agency for the current location. NO adjustment is made for differences in wind speed averaging periods. hurdat/atcf = North Atlantic - U.S. Miami (NOAA NHC) - 1-minute winds tokyo = RSMC Tokyo (JMA) - 10-minute newdelhi = RSMC New Delhi (IMD) - 3-minute reunion = RSMC La Reunion (MFLR) - 10 minute bom = Australian TCWCs (TCWC Perth/nDarwin/nBrisbane) - 10-minute nadi = RSMC Nadi (FMS) - 10 minute wellington = TCWC Wellington (NZMS) - 10-minute
Column name: usa_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: Minimum central pressure (mb)
Column name: tokyo_r30_short Type: NUMBER Description: The shortest radius of 30kt winds or greater
