Column name: nadi_longitude Type: FLOAT Description: Longitude from Fiji Meteorological Service data from RSMC Hadi
Column name: tokyo_r50_short Type: NUMBER Description: The shortest radius of 50kt winds or greater
Column name: usa_r34_ne Type: NUMBER Description: – 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: bom_pressure_method Type: NUMBER Description: This code may need to be expanded to handle new systems in the future/nand also to differentiate between pressure-wind relationships used to derive the central pressure. ADAM code Method WMO Code NULL Unknown or N/A 1 Aircraft or Dropsonde  observation 1 2 Over water observation (e.g.  buoy) 2 3 Over land observation 3 4 Instrument – unknown type 5 5 Derived Directly from DVORAK 4 6 Derived from wind via a P-W  equation 5 7 Estimate from surrounding obs 5 8 Extrapolation from radar 5 9 Other 5
Column name: usa_rmw Type: NUMBER Description: radius of max winds/n0 - 999 n mi. NOT BEST TRACKED (not reanalyzed)
Column name: mlc_pressure Type: NUMBER Description: 
Column name: track_type Type: TEXT Description: Track type Tropical storms can interact. This identifies : PROVISIONAL - Real time data used to populate the position and other parameters of this system. This is a provisional track that will be replaced when reanalysis of the storm is performed. (Usually within 2 years of the storm's occurence) main - primary track associated with a storm system. spur - usually short lived tracks associated with a main track and either represent alternate positions at the beginning of a system. Can also represent actual system interactions (e.g./nFujiwhara interactions).
Column name: ds824_latitude Type: FLOAT Description: Latitude from DataSet 824 - A historic dataset with data from the 1800s through 1980(ish)
Column name: usa_record Type: TEXT Description: Record identifier (see notes below) C – Closest approach to a coast/nnot followed by a landfall G – Genesis I – An intensity peak in terms of both pressure and wind L – Landfall (center of system crossing a coastline) P – Minimum in central pressure R – Provides additional detail on the intensity of the cyclone when rapid changes are underway S – Change of status of the system T – Provides additional detail on the track (position) of the cyclone W – Maximum sustained wind speed
Column name: reunion_r64_nw Type: NUMBER Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: usa_r64_sw Type: NUMBER Description: – 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: tokyo_grade Type: NUMBER Description: <Grade> 1 : Not used  2 : Tropical Depression (TD)  3 : Tropical Storm (TS)  4 : Severe Tropical Storm (STS)  5 : Typhoon (TY)  6 : Extratropical Cyclone (L)  7 : Just entering into the responsible area of  Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA)  8 : Not used  9 : Tropical Cyclone of TS intensity or higher
Column name: newdelhi_latitude Type: FLOAT Description: 
